# Architecture Boundaries

Ports-and-adapters layering defined in master plan §2.6; repository layout in §3. Cargo virtual workspace,
all library crates flat under `crates/` (M-CRATES-FLAT-FOLDER), thin binaries under `apps/` plus `xtask/`.

## Layers (dependencies point inward, graph is acyclic)

| Layer | Prefix / examples | May depend on | Must not depend on |
|---|---|---|---|
| Foundation | `cms-types`, `php-value`, `php-serialize`, `cms-contracts` | std, small vetted crates | any workspace layer |
| Domain | `cms-hooks`, `cms-db`, `cms-query`, `cms-content`, … | foundation | VM, DB drivers, HTTP, async runtime, `infra-*`, `platform-*` |
| Orchestration | `cms-request`, `cms-bootstrap` | domain, foundation | VM, `infra-*` |
| PHP runtime | `php-vm-adapter`, `php-abi-bridge` | foundation | domain, orchestration |
| PHP bindings | `php-bindings` | domain, runtime, foundation | `infra-*`, `platform-*` |
| Infrastructure | `infra-mysql`, `infra-http`, `infra-fs`, … | domain ports, foundation | orchestration, platform, other `infra-*` |
| Platform | `platform-server`, `platform-telemetry`, … | orchestration, domain ports, foundation | concrete `infra-*` (injected instead) |
| Binaries | `apps/*`, `xtask` | everything | — nothing depends on a binary |
| Test support | `test-harness` | anything, as a **dev-dependency only** | being a normal dependency of production crates |

## Core ↔ PHP without a cycle
- Domain crates hold VM-neutral handles from `php-value` and call PHP through its invocation port.
- `php-abi-bridge` implements that port; `php-bindings` registers the PHP-visible WordPress API by
  delegating to the native owner. Domain crates never import the bridge or the VM.

## Hard boundaries
- **VM isolation:** VM types never appear outside `php-vm-adapter` / `php-abi-bridge` (M-DONT-LEAK-TYPES).
- **Single owner per behavior:** one domain crate owns each WordPress behavior; never reimplement it in
  bindings or a second crate.
- **Ports live with their consumer:** the domain crate that needs a capability defines the trait;
  `infra-*` implements it.
- **Composition roots only in binaries:** library crates never construct DB pools, runtimes, clocks or VMs.
- **Reference lab isolation:** nothing under `lab/` or reference PHP/WordPress source is a dependency of,
  or copied into, a production crate or image.
- **Contracts are data:** `contracts/` holds versioned specs; code references contract IDs, never redefines them.

## Module hygiene
- One public path per item (M-SINGLE-ITEM-PATH); no glob re-exports; no preludes.
- Default private; `pub(crate)` before `pub`; keep `unreachable_pub` clean.
- No grab-bag crates or modules (`common`, `utils`, `helpers`, `misc`, `security`).
- Split files that grow past one coherent concern (~500 lines is a review trigger).

## Changing a boundary
Adding a crate, moving a crate between layers, or adding a cross-layer dependency requires an ADR in
`docs/adr/NNNN-title.md` before code lands.
